# UI copy casing

English labels, headers, titles, buttons, and similar chrome use **title case**. Running prose
stays **sentence case**. Spanish, French, and Greek follow each language's own capitalization.
Do not copy English title case into those catalogs.

## Title case

Capitalize the first word, the last word, and the other words. In the middle of the phrase,
lowercase articles, coordinating conjunctions, and prepositions:

`a`, `an`, `the`, `and`, `but`, `or`, `nor`, `as`, `at`, `by`, `for`, `from`, `in`, `into`,
`of`, `off`, `on`, `onto`, `over`, `to`, `with`, `via`, `per`

```text
GOOD  My Clips · Add Feed · Mark as Played · Add by RSS · Go to Track · Sign Up · On the Tab Bar
BAD   My clips · Add feed · Mark as played · Add By RSS · Go To Track · On The Tab Bar
```

This applies to buttons, screen and section titles, navigation and tab labels, menu rows, table
headers, form labels, modal titles, chips, short status labels, empty-state headings, page
titles, SEO titles, and accessibility names that name a control.

Search and filter placeholders that name the field follow the same rule (`Search by Title...`).

## Sentence case

Full sentences, help text, descriptions, confirmation questions, error paragraphs, SEO
descriptions, and instructional placeholders stay sentence case. Capitalize the first character
and proper nouns only.

```text
GOOD  Log in to use this feature. · Type your email · At least 8 characters
BAD   Log In to Use This Feature. · Type Your Email
```

## What stays capitalized

Proper nouns keep their own capitalization wherever they appear:

- **Brands and products:** Podverse, Podcast Index, Metaboost, Lightning, Bitcoin, Alby, Nostr,
  PayPal, Stripe, Apple, Google, F-Droid, CarPlay, Android Auto, Discord, Mastodon, Matrix,
  Next.js, Buy Me a Coffee, Unified Push, Web Push.
- **Acronyms and initialisms:** RSS, OPML, URL, ID, API, HTML, V4V, LNURL, FOSS, GB, USD.
- **Membership tier names:** Premium, Trial (`Buy Premium Membership`, `Your Trial status has …`).
- **Taxonomy category names** (`categories.*`): keep the directory spelling, including `How To`
  and `Education for Kids`.
- **Keyboard key names** (`settings.keyboard.*`): Space, Arrow Left, Enter, Escape.
- **A control named inside a sentence** uses the same title case as the control:
  `press the "Add Feed" button`.

Legal documents under `apps/api/legal/**` are authored prose, not UI chrome.

## Where this applies

- `packages/i18n-catalog/*/originals/en-US.json` — the authoring source. Web, mobile, and
  management-web inherit it. Get chrome right here.
- `packages/i18n-catalog/*/originals/{es,fr,el-GR}.json` and `overrides/*` — each language's own
  capitalization. Do not mirror English title case.
- Hardcoded copy that has not moved into the catalog yet. See **i18n-user-facing-strings**.
- E2E text assertions (`getByRole({ name })`, `getByText`, Maestro `text:`) must match the
  shipped copy exactly. Playwright's default name matching is case-insensitive, so a stale
  assertion can pass while lying about the product — update it anyway.

Route and tab **identifiers** (`'My Library'` in `tabLayout.ts` / navigation param lists) are
code, not copy. Leave them; the visible label comes from the catalog.

## This is the standard

Write new English chrome in title case. Do not stop to ask, and do not file a button, title, or
label as sentence case. A one-off sentence-case label is something the operator has to ask for.
